-- Rifts World Book 34: Northern Gun Two, four power armors (printed 123-133): Midas, Night Reaper, Pit Fighter, Prophet
-- 4 vehicle rows, with 38 locations and 22 weapon entries.
--
-- One-off data script, run once per environment. NOT a migration - it adds
-- rows, not schema.
--
--   node scripts/d1-apply.mjs --local apps/character-creator/db/~309-northern-gun-2-power-armor-f.sql
--
-- Written by scripts/vessel-sql.mjs from 1 worker file(s). Every value
-- is printable ASCII, every row cites its book, and a Main Body location
-- agrees with its vehicle's mdc_main_body.

INSERT OR IGNORE INTO vehicles (slug, name, system, vehicle_class, crew, passengers, speed_ground, speed_air, speed_water, dimensions, weight_tons, mdc_main_body, is_mega_damage, ar, cost, cost_note, description, source_book) VALUES
  ('ng-x16-midas', 'Midas Power Armor', 'rifts', 'power-armor', 'One.', NULL, 'Running: 100 mph (160 km) maximum, at 20% of the normal fatigue rate at high speed and 10% at 70 mph (112 km) or less. Leaping: 20 ft (6.1 m) high or across without the boosters; the lower-leg booster jets carry it 100 ft (30.5 m) high and 150 ft (45.7 m) across; each +30% with a running start; none of it is flight.', 'None; too top- and back-heavy even to hover for a moment.', 'Sinks; walks the bottom at 10 mph (16 km/8.6 knots). Maximum depth 1,000 ft (305 m).', 'Oversized: height 12 ft (3.7 m) to the top of the laser cannon, 11 ft (3.4 m) to the top of the head; width 5 ft (1.5 m); length 4 ft (1.2 m)', '683 lbs (307 kg)', 270, 1, NULL, 640000, '1.3 million credits nuclear, 925,000 Solid Oxide, 640,000 electric battery; the lowest is stored. The giant Vibro-Blade pole arm comes with the suit; sold alone it is 215,000 credits (gear row ng-x16-midas-giant-vibro-blade).', 'Model Type: NG-X16. Class: Armored Infantry Assault Suit. From the BDJP design group (Perry Jones, Nolen Keith and Andy McElvary) and in some ways the Samson''s successor: an oversized robotic shell, like the Samson and Delilah, that seats the pilot high inside a 12 ft frame with comparable armor. Its main gun is a long-range laser cannon in a back turret that fires on voice command or comes out to be used by hand, and, being an energy weapon, needs no heavy ammunition drum. Lighter guns sit in each forearm. Every suit also comes with an outsized silver-plated melee weapon, a halberd, battle axe or big Vibro-Blade, whose edges are Vibro-Blades fed through power connectors in the hands (an idea taken from Triax armor). An all-round heavy assault suit for infantry support, monster hunting and close combat that shoots its targets down at range and then closes in. Once weighed for Xiticix hive raids, it proved too big for them and better at covering troops pulling out of the hives and at border defense. It sells well on the open market, and its big blades sell on their own to Combat Cyborgs, large D-Bees and other power armor owners. Robot P.S. 30. Cargo: none. Power: nuclear, 10 year average life; Solid Oxide and electric battery versions are priced. Handheld weapons: oversized guns and blades made for big robots, heavy power armor and Combat Cyborgs, since ordinary man-sized weapons are too small for its hands. Extra weapons ride in hand, on a shoulder strap or in a carrying bag, and a big Vibro-Sword or similar backup can hang in a scabbard at the waist. Hand to hand per Basic or Elite Ground-Based Power Armor Training (Rifts Ultimate Edition p.351-352): restrained punch 1D4 M.D., full punch 1D6, power punch 2D6 (two attacks), kick 2D4, leap kick 2D8 (two attacks). Sensors and features: the standard set only. Cat-like landings: its leg thrusters set it down safely from as high as 300 ft (91.4 m); from 300 to 600 ft (183 m) roll 1D20, on 1-10 the suit takes 4D6 M.D. and the pilot loses 1D4 melee actions, on 11-20 no harm or delay; higher drops do 2D6x10 M.D. to the suit, 6D6 S.D.C./Hit Points to the wearer and stun him 1D4 melee rounds. Losing the lower-leg jets ends booster leaps.', 'Rifts World Book 34: Northern Gun Two p.123-125'),
  ('ng-uelx45-night-reaper', 'Night Reaper Light Power Armor', 'rifts', 'power-armor', 'One.', NULL, 'Running: 50 mph (80 km) maximum, reached from a standstill in 24 seconds, at 10% of the normal fatigue rate. Leaping: 12 ft (3.7 m) high or across. Climbing: its strength adds +5% to Climbing and Spelunking and +3% to Acrobatics and Gymnastics, and its climb grippers add another +3% to Climbing and Spelunking.', 'None, unless fitted with a back jet pack or a glider like the Silent Shadow''s, either at extra cost.', 'Swims 10 mph (16 km) or walks the bottom at 5 mph (8 km/4.3 knots), at 20% of the normal fatigue rate. Maximum depth 400 ft (122 m).', 'Man-sized: height 5.6-7 ft (1.7 to 2.1 m); width 2-3 ft (0.6 to 0.9 m); length 2 ft (0.6 m)', '124 lbs (56 kg)', 150, 1, NULL, 398000, '950,000 credits nuclear, 650,000 Solid Oxide, 398,000 electric battery; the lowest is stored. The Vibro-Scythe comes with the suit, and Northern Gun sells it no other way. An extra thigh UEL is 160,000 more (gear row ng-uelx45-thigh-uel).', 'Model Type: NG-UELX45. Class: Light Strategic Espionage Power Armor with UEL system. A stealth suit from Team Manning (Nenad Petrovic, Matthew Powell, Trent Slater and A.B. Manning) for spies, saboteurs, special forces and night operations, trading heavy plating and guns for quiet, agility and good night optics. Like the Sabre it carries no built-in weapons to unbalance it or catch on things, and it is so smooth and slim it can pass for Bushman body armor. Sold in black, dark grey, navy blue and camouflage. Its buyers turned out to be far more varied than NG planned: scouts, police, militias, investigators, explorers, scientists and adventurers, but above all the underworld of assassins, burglars, smugglers, pirates and terrorists, and NG argues privately over whether to stop making a suit that could be turned on its own secrets, so far choosing to keep selling it at a handsome profit. Robot P.S. 22. Cargo: none. Power: nuclear, 15 year average life; Solid Oxide and electric battery versions are priced. Handheld weapons only, usually energy weapons fed by the UEL; a side arm, Vibro-Blade and other gear go on a belt, a shoulder sling or a backpack. UEL (2, one under plating in each forearm): a cable and E-Clip connector that powers a weapon of up to 1D6x10 M.D. a blast, with a breaker that shuts off anything stronger. Hand to hand per Basic or Elite Ground-Based Power Armor Training (Rifts Ultimate Edition p.351-352), as printed: restrained punch 6D6 M.D. (so printed, above the 1D4 M.D. normal punch; most likely S.D.C.), normal punch 1D4 M.D., power punch 2D4 (two attacks), kick 1D6, leap kick 2D6 (two attacks). Features beyond the standard: a garrote strangle cord at the left wrist, also usable for climbing; a hidden left-arm compartment, under its upper plate, sized for a small lock pick kit, 2-4 shuriken or climbing cord; retractable climb grippers in the palms, fingers and boots, too small to fight with; rubber soles and padded plates that muffle its movement, so Prowl, Climbing, Swim, Acrobatics, Gymnastics and the like suffer none of the usual armor penalty; goggle-eye multi-optics with passive nightvision and infrared (1,600 ft/488 m), ultraviolet (400 ft/122 m), telescopic sight (2 miles/3.2 km), x12 macro and a camera holding 100 hours of video and 4,000 stills; a mouthpiece loudspeaker with language translator and 20-voice modulator; and audio amplification equal to a Combat Cyborg''s Amplified Hearing.', 'Rifts World Book 34: Northern Gun Two p.126-127'),
  ('ng-gccpa-03-pit-fighter', 'Pit Fighter Power Armor', 'rifts', 'power-armor', 'One.', NULL, 'Running: 30 mph (48 km) maximum, at 20% of the normal fatigue rate; each extra 10 mph (16 km) costs 30,000 credits, to a maximum of 60 mph (96 km). Leaping: 10 ft (3 m) high or across; each extra 5 ft (1.5 m) costs 10,000 credits, to a maximum of 20 ft (6.1 m). Jump jets in both legs (80,000 credits) raise leaps to 50 ft (15.2 m) high or across, +20% with a running start.', 'None; it can neither hover nor fly.', 'Sinks; walks the bottom at 5 mph (8 km/4.3 knots). Depth tolerance 400 ft (122 m).', 'Height 6-10 ft (1.8 to 3 m); width 2-4 ft (0.6 to 1.2 m); length 2.5-4 ft (0.76 to 1.2 m); each by the buyer''s size and the weapons, frills and cosmetic pieces fitted', '300-700 lbs (135 to 315 kg), by the final design', 100, 1, NULL, 600000, 'A typical new, fully powered suit is 600,000 to 1.6 million credits, by power supply, extra M.D.C., speed, P.S., cosmetics and weapons; the low end is stored. Power supply: nuclear 700,000-800,000, Solid Oxide 450,000, electric battery 200,000. Upgrades: +10 Main Body M.D.C. per 25,000 to 180; +10 mph per 30,000 to 60 mph; +5 ft of leap per 10,000 to 20 ft; leg jump jets 80,000; +1 Robot P.S. per 4,000 from 20 to 26. Faceplate and helmet pieces 100-400 each; animated, spinning, smoking or blood-spraying pieces 1,000-4,000. Built-in blades by size: knife-size or smaller Vibro-Blades, spikes and horns 4,000-7,000 each; Vibro-Knives 6,000-7,000 (3,000 more if retractable); short swords and like-sized horns 9,000; larger swords 10,000-12,000; giant Vibro-Weapons 16,000-20,000, usually handheld. Combat Cyborg-style alternatives cost 20% more. The lettered optional weapons are gear rows of their own (slugs ng-gccpa-03-...).', 'Model Type: GCCPA-03 (headed NG-GCCPA-03). Class: Gladiatorial Close Combat Arena Powered Armor. Northern Gun''s answer to the Robodome and the spread of arenas, fighting pits and death games across North America, designed by Kenneth Merrow, Christopher Spencer, Neil Wage and Carm N. Bellaire: buyers get a basic frame and then customize nearly everything, from plating, helmet and face to shoulder and forearm weapons, paint and ornament, each a separate purchase. Shatter armor: the suit is covered in small scale-like plates made to break off in a fight so the crowd can see damage land; they mean nothing to how the suit works. A removable faceplate in a samurai spirit comes as a stern or screaming warrior, bull or moose, demon, dog, cat, insect, reptile, brute or robot, and can be dressed up with moustaches, beards, hair, brows, goggles, horns, fins and spikes, of carved M.D.C. material or artificial hair, some able to change expression. It is built for show and close fighting in the arena rather than war or adventuring, so most of its weapons are short-ranged or handheld, with a few heavy ones for spectacle. Mounting limits: per forearm, an energy weapon and a melee weapon; a single weapon on the shoulders and a single one on the head; and one set of Vibro-Spikes on each shoulder, elbow, forearm, knee, shin and the helmet top. Any energy rifle, pistol or melee weapon its hands can hold may be used, though thick armored fingers need cyborg- or power armor-sized weapons, and each arena sets its own rules. Robot P.S. 20 to start, raised at a price to 26. Cargo: a small store for extra supplies and personal weapons. Power: nuclear, 12 year average life, or Solid Oxide or electric battery. Hand to hand per Ground-Based Power Armor Training (Rifts Ultimate Edition p.352), damage by its Robot P.S. (Rifts Ultimate Edition p.285). Features: the standard Northern Gun set plus a basic helmet fight camera recording the bout from the fighter''s view, for broadcast or video extras.', 'Rifts World Book 34: Northern Gun Two p.128-130'),
  ('ng-x67-prophet', 'Prophet Power Armor', 'rifts', 'power-armor', 'One.', NULL, 'Running: 90 mph (144 km) maximum, at 20% of the normal fatigue rate and 10% below 50 mph (80 km). Leaping: 15 ft (4.6 m) high or across unassisted; the lower-leg jump jets carry it 100 ft (30.5 m) high or across; each +50% with a running start. Not flight. VTOL leaps: the same jets lift it straight up or down to upper floors and rooftops and onto giant foes. Power jumping travel is not possible.', 'None; it cannot even hover.', 'Swims or walks the bottom at 10 mph (16 km/8.6 knots), at 20% of the normal fatigue rate. Maximum depth 500 ft (152 m).', 'Man-sized, by the wearer: height 5.6-8 ft (1.7 to 2.4 m); width 3-4 ft (0.9 to 1.2 m); length 2-4 ft (0.6 to 1.2 m)', '308 lbs (138.6 kg)', 175, 1, NULL, 500000, '1.2 million credits nuclear, 865,000 Solid Oxide, 500,000 electric battery; the lowest is stored. Silver plating each forearm Vibro-Blade is 2,500 more (gear row ng-x67-prophet-silver-plating).', 'Model Type: NG-X67. Class: Law Enforcement Surveillance, Investigation and Espionage Troop Support Power Armor. Designed by Joel Rodriguez, Christopher Spencer and Rawson Hallect, first for police work, from features borrowed off other suits plus some new ones; it serves military police, special forces, surveillance, investigators, bounty and monster hunters, vampire slayers, search and rescue and infantry support. The name comes from its cameras, sensors and computers, which watch every direction and help the wearer read and anticipate what enemies will do, feeding recognition software for investigation and combat; with radar and sonar, multi-optics and long-range communications it suits crime scene and detective work as well as most combat roles. The head is not its weak point: optics and bonuses survive until all four sensor/communication nodes are destroyed, pilots keep one or two backup tinted goggles whose wireless HUD still shows the camera feeds, and the backpack''s portable scanners and communications restore radar and communications to that HUD; only with all of these gone is the pilot reduced to his own senses. Special bonuses: +1 on Perception Rolls, +2 to automatic dodge, +1 to roll with impact, and it cannot be snuck up on or surprised from behind. Robot P.S. 26. Cargo: none. Power: nuclear, 12 year average life; Solid Oxide and electric battery versions are priced. Standard handheld kit: an NG energy pistol and an NG energy rifle, shotgun or over-and-under (energy barrel over a grenade launcher), with room for a Vibro-Blade, Neural Mace or backup gun, grenades and flares on belts, in a bag or backpack, or slung. UEL (2, one under plating in each forearm): a cable and E-Clip connector giving any E-Clip weapon unlimited payload. Hand to hand per Basic or Elite Ground-Based Power Armor Training (Rifts Ultimate Edition p.351-352): restrained punch 1D4 M.D., full punch 1D6, power punch 2D6 (two attacks), kick 2D4, leap kick 2D8 (two attacks). Features beyond the standard: an optional Criminal I.D. Recognition System, new and experimental but right 89% of the time, matching faces, tattoos, scars and gang colors against up to 250,000 known criminals, fugitives, bounties and dangerous beings, and anyone else whose picture is loaded; an advanced camera in the right temple with a 2 mile (3.2 km) telescopic zoom and x12 macro lens that transmits live 5 miles (8 km) and stores 96 hours of video and 8,000 stills; eight plain dash-cams (two in the forehead, two in the chest, one in each forearm, two in the backpack) storing 48 hours and 4,000 stills each; two peekaboo cameras on bendable arms behind the shoulders that unfold to look behind, around corners or through foliage (as described for the Forester); a detachable flashlight beside the right shoulder (4 M.D.C., 200 ft/61 m); an oversized hard-shell backpack (the features text says 35 M.D.C., the location table 45) holding two gallons (7.5 liters) of water, a first aid kit, a Portable Computer Field Unit and a Portable Scan Dihilator (Rifts Ultimate Edition p.162 and 164); an eyeless Cyclopean helmet that shows everything on its HUD, its central rotating eye a camera and sensor cluster with a laser distancer and a black light for ultraviolet markings; a forehead lamp that follows the gaze (120 ft/36.6 m) with an infrared light to its right; multi-optics with passive nightvision and infrared (1,600 ft/488 m), ultraviolet (400 ft/122 m), telescopic sight (2 miles/3.2 km) and x12 macro; a mouthpiece loudspeaker with language translator and 20-voice modulator; and a proximity warning like the White Knight''s that announces anything within 100 ft (30.5 m), shows it on request, names it through the recognition system where it can, and is silenced by telling it the contact is friendly.', 'Rifts World Book 34: Northern Gun Two p.131-133');

INSERT OR IGNORE INTO vehicle_locations (vehicle_slug, location, mdc, mdc_note, ordinal) VALUES
